%!
% Splat!
% 
% Warning:
% 
% This does weird things if there are SunView1 windows on the screen.
% When you run this your SunView1 windows will dissappear. (good riddance!)
% Whenever any of the SunView1 windows move or change size, the NeWS
% framebuffer is reshaped so there are holes in it for the SunView1 
% windows to show through. But since this code reshapes the framebuffer 
% without taking into consideration any of the SunView1 windows, NeWS
% starts drawing on top where they would be. But fortunatly, they still 
% seem to be there. When you move one of them around, it will reset the 
% framebuffer shape, and undo our little bit of vandalism. 
% 
% Nobody's responsible for anything done with this program!
% Don't use this on unsuspecting people, that would be naughty.

/inner 30 def
/outer 200 def
/spaz 20 def
/twist 20 def

% Make another framebuffer not subjected to clipping restrictions.
{(FRAMEBUFFER) getenv} errored {pop (/dev/fb)} if createdevice
setcanvas

clippath pathbbox points2rect /h exch def /w exch def
pop pop

matrix currentmatrix
w random mul h random mul translate

inner random mul inner add 0 moveto
360 twist idiv 2 mul {
  outer random mul inner add spaz dup add random mul spaz sub 
  lineto
  inner random mul inner add 0 lineto
  twist rotate
} repeat

closepath 

setmatrix
gsave
  0 0 w h rectpath
  framebuffer eoreshapecanvas
grestore
gsave
  random random random dup mul sethsbcolor
  fill
  grestore
0 setgray
4 setlinewidth
stroke
